            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0329" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9191: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-04T12:00:00+08:00">August 4,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>367. Shanghai’s 418, August 3, 10 p.m. I spent yesterday in Shanghai and
                    discussed matter set forth in above telegram with <pb facs="0330" n="323"
                        xml:id="pg323"/> Gauss. I agree with his estimate of the situation. It
                    occurs to me that something might be accomplished by the powers by
                    representations at Tokyo and Nanking suggesting that both countries agree to the
                    elimination of the Shanghai area from war activities somewhat along lines taken
                    by the four diplomatic representatives at Peiping as quoted in Peiping’s 312,
                    July 28, 2 p.m., and as contemplated by Department’s 138, July 27, noon to
                        Peiping.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d347-f1"/></p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d347-f1" n="40" xml:id="d347-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed. See telegram No. 128, July 27, 1 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    Japan, <ref target="frus1937v04#pg_238">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >iv</hi>, p. 238</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
